From 5795eafd8d9a44be89ad7fd9fc0fd735529882e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 13:00:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 67/83] libm: 80-bit erf/gamma/Bessel + complex special
 functions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reimplement the remaining long-double special functions that cast through
double (losing range and accuracy) in genuine x87 80-bit, calling the
existing 80-bit scalars (expl/logl/sinl/cosl/sqrtl) — no double cast on any
value path.

- lgammal/lgammal_r/tgammal: Stirling asymptotic + recurrence (push x>16 via
  lnΓ(x)=lnΓ(x+1)-ln x, then an 8-term Bernoulli series with exact rational
  constants); reflection for x<0.5; signgam from floor(x) parity.  lgammal_r
  now lives in mathl.c (the old double-cast in math_reentrant.c is removed —
  single definition, no link collision).
- erfl/erfcl: three-region split with no lossy cancellation — Maclaurin
  series (|x|<1.5), modified-Lentz continued fraction (1.5-6), asymptotic
  series (>=6).
- j0l/j1l/y0l/y1l/jnl/ynl: long-double ascending power series for small |x|
  and Hankel P/Q asymptotic for large |x|, mirroring the double recurrence
  structure.
- Complex clgammal/ctgammal/cerfl/cerfcl/cj0l/cj1l/cy0l/cy1l: computed on
  long-double real/imag parts (no double-complex cast).

Verified vs the host's 80-bit libm, including out-of-double-range cases that
prove the range fix: tgammal(1000.5)=1.272e2566 (was inf), erfcl(50)=
2.07e-1088 (was 0), lgammal(1e30)=6.808e31; moderate-range accuracy 15-19
sig digits (erfl was ~7 with the old A&S double cast).  Special values
(poles, ±Inf, NaN, FE_* flags) match the double contract.  Double path
untouched: tests/lib/m test_bessel/prop_bessel still 0 failures / 122/122.

Known residual (documented in source): complex cerfl/cerfcl for |z|>~5 and
complex Bessel for |z|>~30 share the double versions' ascending-series
cancellation; full 80-bit for moderate |z|, and the long-double exponent
range is preserved either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
